second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What political party was Daniel Hogan affiliated with?\", \"slot_hint\": \"political_party\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 107, \"text\": \"He was at many of Grant's major battles, including Fort Henry, Fort Donelson, Corinth, Nashville, and Iuka.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d00\", \"start\": 108, \"end\": 224, \"text\": \"He was mustered out at the close of the war, whereupon he attended the business school at Bryant & Stratton College.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d00\", \"start\": 225, \"end\": 289, \"text\": \"After graduation, he worked for Western Union in several cities.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d00\", \"start\": 290, \"end\": 365, \"text\": \"He returned to Mound City, Illinois in 1869 to attend to his aging parents.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d00\", \"start\": 366, \"end\": 449, \"text\": \"In 1873, Hogan was elected Pulaski County Clerk, holding the office for nine years.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d00\", \"start\": 450, \"end\": 494, \"text\": \"Hogan purchased the Pulaski Patriot in 1880.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d00\", \"start\": 495, \"end\": 561, \"text\": \"In 1882, Hogan was elected as a Republican to the Illinois Senate.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d00\", \"start\": 562, \"end\": 587, \"text\": \"He was re-elected in each\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 17, \"text\": \"and Republicans .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d01\", \"start\": 18, \"end\": 51, \"text\": \"It ’ s more important than that .\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d01\", \"start\": 52, \"end\": 142, \"text\": \"This is a fight for Maryland and America ’ s future , and that is a fight worth fighting .\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d01\", \"start\": 143, \"end\": 314, \"text\": \"And that ’ s why I have made the decision to run for the United States Senate – not to serve one party – but to fix our nation ’ s broken politics and fight for Maryland .\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d01\", \"start\": 315, \"end\": 421, \"text\": \"It ’ s what I did as your governor , and it ’ s exactly how I ’ ll serve you in the United States Senate .\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d01\", \"start\": 422, \"end\": 433, \"text\": \"Let ’ s get\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 191, \"text\": \") District 7 Eric Burlison ( R ) District 8 Jason Smith ( R ) Republican Party ( 8 ) Democratic Party ( 2 ) v • e State of Missouri Jefferson City ( capital ) Elections What 's on my ballot ?\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d02\", \"start\": 192, \"end\": 298, \"text\": \"| Elections in 2025 | How to vote | How to run for office | Ballot measures Government Who represents me ?\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d02\", \"start\": 299, \"end\": 305, \"text\": \"| U.S.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0091-4b6bfd5926d4:d02\", \"start\": 306, \"end\": 322, \"text\": \"President | U.S.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_n